clinic for advice regarding starting combined
Oral contraceptive pills (COCPs). You take a
careful medical and family history, which is
Significant for gastroesophageal reflux
disease (GERD) and premenstrual headaches.
She has smoked 15-20 cigarettes a day for
the past four years and drinks 2 to 3 glasses
of wine every day. Her family history includes
breast cancer in her mother, diagnosed at the
age of 53 years, and hypertension in her
father. On examination, her blood pressure is
130/78 mmHg. She has a body mass index
(BMI) of 28. She wants to know if there is
anything wrong with her taking OCPs. In
counseling her, which of the following will you
discuss further as a possible absolute
contraindication to COCPs?','{"A":"Her drinking history.","B":"Her family history of breast cancer.","C":"Her premenstrual headaches.","D":"Her BMI.","E":"Her smoking history. ©"}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (4).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-640e6e036326","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"6c8d6059d37f0fa1583d","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (4).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (4).pdf","source_page":49,"source_qid":null},{"record_id":"cb524e1707809428417a","record_type":"visual_mcq","source_file":"Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Obstetrics and Gynaecology Amedex 2025.pdf","source_page":42,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"five_block_inferred","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high','{"record_id":"6c8d6059d37f0fa1583d","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (4).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 GYNAECOLOGY (4).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":49,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Gynaecology","stem":"Dorothy, 21 years of age, presents to your GP\nclinic for advice regarding starting combined\nOral contraceptive pills (COCPs). You take a\ncareful medical and family history, which is\nSignificant for gastroesophageal reflux\ndisease (GERD) and premenstrual headaches.\nShe has smoked 15-20 cigarettes a day for\nthe past four years and drinks 2 to 3 glasses\nof wine every day. Her family history includes\nbreast cancer in her mother, diagnosed at the\nage of 53 years, and hypertension in her\nfather. On examination, her blood pressure is\n130/78 mmHg. She has a body mass index\n(BMI) of 28. She wants to know if there is\nanything wrong with her