year-old man, who is a known case of sickle cell
disease, presents to the emergency department
with severe right calf pain. The pain started
acutely two hours ago and is 6 out of 10 ona
scale of 1 to 10, according to the patient. He
denies any chest pain or shortness of breath.
On examination, he has a blood pressure of
134/78 mmHg, pulse rate of 98 bpm, respiratory
rate of 17 breaths/min, a temperature of 37.2°C,
and O2 saturation of 94% on room air. Chest
examination is normal and there is no abnormal
respiratory or heart sound. Which one of the
following would be the next best step in
management?','{"A":"Enoxaparin.","B":"Adequate analgesia.","C":"Oxygen.","D":"Hydration.","E":"Limb elevation."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[29],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-d570b1c173e7","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"324cf0238bdeef471fe0","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":29,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"v27_same_page_five_structural","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"324cf0238bdeef471fe0","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":29,"supporting_pages":[29],"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"After a long flight from London to Sydney, a 35-\nyear-old man, who is a known case of sickle cell\ndisease, presents to the emergency department\nwith severe right calf pain. The pain started\nacutely two hours ago and is 6 out of 10 ona\nscale of 1 to 10, according to the patient. He\ndenies any chest pain or shortness of breath.\nOn examination, he has a blood pressure of\n134/78 mmHg, pulse rate of 98 bpm, respiratory\nrate of 17 breaths/min, a temperature of 37.2°C,\nand O2 saturation of 94% on room air. Chest\nexamination is normal and there is no abnormal\nrespiratory or heart sound. Which one of the\nfollowing would be the next best step in\nmanagement?","options":{"A":"Enoxaparin.","B":"Adequate analgesia.","C":"Oxygen.","D":"Hydration.","E":"Limb elevation."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verificatio