is brought to the emergency department. The
wife mentions that her husband woke up
with a nagging headache. One hour later, he
Started to develop slurred speech and
weakness in the right arm. She mentioned
that her husband has been on a pill for his
cardiac condition for the past 3 months, but
She cannot remember the name. Since his
pulse seems irregular, you assume that the
pill is warfarin and check an INR, which comes
back to 4.5. A non-contrast CT scan of the
head reveals intracranial hemorrhage. Which
one of the following is the next best action to
take?','{"A":"Give fresh frozen plasma (FFP).","B":"Give FFP and vitamin K.","C":"Give protamine sulfate.","D":"Give vitamin K.","E":"Switch to unfractionated heparin."}',NULL,NULL,'{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-8f94e63ba8fe","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"04230b486516e4d43d60","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_page":98,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"tesseract_retry_200dpi_psm3","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"04230b486516e4d43d60","source_file":"AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX 2025.09更新包/AMEDEX 2025 HEMAETOLOGY (2).pdf","source_year":2025,"source_page":98,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"Accompanied by his wife, a 68-year-old man\nis brought to the emergency department. The\nwife mentions that her husband woke up\nwith a nagging headache. One hour later, he\nStarted to develop slurred speech and\nweakness in the right arm. She mentioned\nthat her husband has been on a pill for his\ncardiac condition for the past 3 months, but\nShe cannot remember the name. Since his\npulse seems irregular, you assume that the\npill is warfarin and check an INR, which comes\nback to 4.5. A non-contrast CT scan of the\nhead reveals intracranial hemorrhage. Which\none of the following is the next best action to\ntake?","options":{"A":"Give fresh frozen plasma (FFP).","B":"Give FFP and vitamin K.","C":"Give protamine sulfate.","D":"Give vitamin K.","E":"Switch to unfractionated heparin."},"source_answer":null,"source_explanation":null,"source_answer_status":"pending_import","current_answer":null,"curr